 #md "# ADR-2606172100: Retire the open-UNSPSC per-code Python agent fleet

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-06-17
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki

# Context

ADR-2605171300 (Open-UNSPSC Generative Agent Fleet) materialized the UNSPSC domain
as **one generated LangGraph agent file per commodity code** —
`crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/langgraph_graphs/unispsc_agents/c{code}.py`,
**18,343 files / ~1.23M LOC** in the kotoba submodule. They were not statically
imported: `__init__.py` was a one-line docstring and modules were resolved at runtime
by `dynamic_runner.py` / `unispsc_organism.py` / `xrpc/unispsc.py` via
`importlib.import_module(f\"...c{code}\")`.

That whole surface is superseded by the **clj `unspsc` actor**
(`orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-unspsc`, on `etzhayyim/root@main`): **one framework + one data table**
(`resources/unspsc-taxonomy.edn`, 18,342 codes) on the `com-junkawasaki/kotodama`
runtime, per the substrate-native Python→Clojure port wave (ADR-2606160842) and the
kotoba Datom substrate (ADR-2605262130). Inference is Murakumo-only (ADR-2605215000).

The Python per-code fleet was therefore dead weight (~1.23M LOC) plus several live
couplings into the crate: the organism runtime, the openUnispsc XRPC server, the MCP
dispatch table, and the kuni-umi planning cells' BoM/specialist fan-out.

# Decision

Retire the Python UNSPSC per-code surface in **staged, independently-reviewable PRs**,
leaf → root, so the tree stays importable and degrades gracefully at every step. Landed
as a 6-PR stack on `com-junkawasaki/kotoba`:

| Step | PR | What |
|------|----|------|
| 1 | #162 | Delete the 18,343 generated per-code agents (`unispsc_agents/c*.py`, ~1.23M LOC) + this retirement's kotoba-internal ADR. Runtime-safe: `dynamic_runner` already treats a missing per-code module as `no_custom_agent_found`. |
| 2 | #168 | Remove Layer B loaders + the UNSPSC domain surface — `dynamic_runner`, `open_unispsc_{pregel,item}`, `primitives/open_unispsc` (1,452 LOC), `xrpc/unispsc`, `unispsc_capabilities/*` + tests. Surgical Layer C decouple in `mcp_dispatch` (drop the `openUnispsc` dispatch entry) + `langgraph_server_app` (drop the xrpc.unispsc router mount). |
| 3 | #164 | Sever the per-code dependency in the organism: `for_code` no longer `import_module`s a deleted `c{code}` module — it builds a generic default classify graph (`no_custom_agent`). |
| 3b | #165 | De-brand: `UnispscOrganism → Organism`, `unispsc_organism.py → organism.py`, `UnispscOrganismFleetCell → OrganismFleetCell`. Pure rename; the generic organism runtime (joucho/cadence/inbox/kaizen/sensors/tick) is unchanged. |
| 4 | #166 | Sweep orphaned data-layer leaves: `unspsc_kotoba_transact.py` + the sqlmesh `mv_open_unispsc_procurement_by_commodity` view. |
| 5 | #167 | Re-point the kuni-umi planning cells (`deployment_planning`, `site_survey`) off the per-code LAN/libp2p executor shards onto the **canonical openUnispsc XRPC gateway** (`unispsc.etzhayyim.com → lg-open-unispsc`); delete the now-backend-less `unispsc_agent_executor` (423 LOC) + `unispsc_registry` (189 LOC) cells + the empty `unispsc_agents` package. |

Each merged step is test-green (`uv run --extra dev pytest`): 90 organism+kaizen tests
after Step 3b, 169 kuni-umi e2e + organism tests after Step 5.

# Consequences

- **~1.5M LOC removed** from the kotoba submodule; `git status` / clone materially lighter.
- Single source of truth for UNSPSC commodity logic becomes the clj actor's data table
  (the contract surface stays the canonical `openUnispsc` XRPC lexicons).
- The kuni-umi BoM/site-survey cells now validate against the canonical, deployed UNSPSC
  XRPC service instead of a bespoke per-code Python fleet; behaviour is unchanged
  (unreachable gateway → synthesized fallback line items, exactly as the dead shards
  already produced).
- **Kept** (NOT retired): the deployed `lg-open-unispsc` langserver (the live backend the
  re-pointed cells now call — it must stay until the clj actor is deployed behind
  `unispsc.etzhayyim.com`); the dual UNSPSC+ISIC MCP (`mcp/unispsc-isic-mcp`, ISIC is a
  live separate taxonomy).
- **Deferred** (operator/infra, not code): the root-repo k8s deploys
  `50-infra/k8s/{unispsc-organism-fleet,lg-open-unispsc}` + the `unispsc-handles` DID
  registry — teardown is a kubectl/ops decision gated on the clj actor's deployment.

